# zaudio.service: realtime stream widths and the speaker volume at boot
# The crackle was SIFS0's mixer at 24 bit (WDMA3 not sign-extended); the driver
# now runs it at 32 bit and 32/32 fits (OTA 29 "D", 19.10: clean). That is
# ~48 dB louder than the broken path. -40 dB was "3-4 of 15" on YouTube: VOL 624 = -24 dB.
RT_WBITS=32
RT_RBITS=32
VOL=624
